---
kind: lore
id: east.gates
title: Eastmarch gates
---

// East answers its own four gates at priority 0, over the spine's
// fallbacks in lore/spine/obstacles.lute (priority -10). Each is eligible
// only while the gate is shut; the engine lets the player through when
// canPass(<gate>) holds.

<entry id="eastGateFerryGangway" on="obstacle" target="gate.ferryGangway" category="bark" when="!holds('canPass', ['ferryGangway'])">
  @meridianSteward{code="0010"}: I'm terribly sorry. The Meridian is by invitation only this season. Mr. Cassius at Tidewell Cape handles the invitations. He's very particular.
</entry>

<entry id="eastGatePortvoltTree" on="obstacle" target="gate.portvoltTree" category="bark" when="!holds('canPass', ['portvoltTree'])">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: A thin, smug-looking tree grows across the east road, right in front of the Spark Gym. A council notice nailed to it reads: TO BE CUT. SOON. It is a year old.
  @narrator{code="0020" when="holds('hasItem', ['hmCut'])"}: You have Cut, but without the Tide Badge your monster won't use it outside battle.
</entry>

<entry id="eastGateRockTunnel" on="obstacle" target="gate.rockTunnel" category="bark" when="!holds('canPass', ['rockTunnel'])">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: The Lantern Tunnel's lamps are long dead. Three steps in, you can't see your own hands. A monster that knows Flash would light the way.
</entry>

<entry id="eastGateAshTowerStairs" on="obstacle" target="gate.ashTowerStairs" category="bark" when="!holds('canPass', ['ashTowerStairs'])">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: Something is standing on the third step. The cold comes off it like off an open door. When you look straight at it, it isn't there, and you can't make your feet climb past it.
</entry>
